{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_012CCaoXZQuis6YneJsyKwyP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder productivity + R&D control system for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A personal productivity system that manages tasks, projects, an inbox, and daily dashboards across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) â€” with markdown files as the single source of truth (no database, plain text, Python stdlib only).\n\n- **What it ships (core app):** `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained stdlib-only Python HTTP server that generates an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading/writing the markdown files directly. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (the one declared deliverable). A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) and a daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) back it up.\n\n- **Task lifecycle:** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored, each with optional notes, surfaced in dashboard views and archive files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`, `domains/*.md`).\n\n- **The larger thrust â€” an R&D \"cockpit\":** Layered on top is a control surface that turns each project's window into a mission-control for trio-driven R&D (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light (green=working Â· amber=needs-you Â· red=crashed Â· grey=idle/done); clicking expands an inline panel â€” never a new page â€” stacking a cached summary on top of a real resizable terminal.\n\n- **What that R&D surface does (v2â†’v4, all built/merged to master):** Persistent server-side terminal sessions over real ConPTY (the lone native dependency, optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, proactive cached project/session summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews on ephemeral ports (hard-guarded â‰  8777), an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-ideas board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Branding/identity:** Presented as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark as the dashboard favicon and masthead.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the project's CLAUDE.md and design docs (which state v4 is built, merged, and 637 tests passing) â€” I haven't independently run the test suite or verified the live service in this turn."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cabd912-ebe7-45d1-a930-5a6d01e58176","uuid":"a0120626-8037-4125-886c-64a834592923","request_id":"req_011Cc1JTBr2ma8U5RUJGdRFG"}
